   "text": "## Growth check: like-for-like, same 12 weeks, year over year\n\n**Basis:** `gross_sales` (quantity × unit price, before returns and tax), each order line counted at the store that rang it up (`order_line.rang_up_at`), summed across stores that were open in both the 2026 and 2025 windows.\n\n**Stores used:** Harbor (S1), Midtown (S2), Eastgate (S3) — all open since 2025-01-01. Northside (S4) is excluded: it opened 2025-07-01, so it wasn't open at all during the year-earlier window.\n\n### Accounting weeks (Sunday–Saturday)\n- 2026 window: Sun 2026-04-05 through Sat 2026-06-27 (12 full weeks) → **$81,625.85**\n- 2025 window: Sun 2025-04-06 through Sat 2025-06-28 (same 12 weeks a year earlier) → **$101,597.06**\n- Change: **-$19,971.21, or -19.66%**\n\n### Operations weeks (Saturday–Friday)\n- 2026 window: Sat 2026-04-04 through Fri 2026-06-26 (last 12 full operations weeks before the Saturday-starting week that hadn't yet closed) → **$81,043.97**\n- 2025 window: Sat 2025-04-05 through Fri 2025-06-27 (same 12 weeks a year earlier) → **$101,272.82**\n- Change: **-$20,228.85, or -19.97%**\n\n**Bottom line:** we are not growing at like-for-like stores. On the accounting-week convention, same-store sales are down about 19.7% year over year; on the operations-week convention they're down about 20.0%. Both conventions agree on the direction and rough magnitude; the small gap between them (19.66% vs 19.97%) comes only from the one-day shift in where each week starts and ends. This is same-store only (Northside's growth as a new store isn't in these figures because it fails the \"open in both periods\" test).\n\nANSWER: No, we are shrinking, not growing: like-for-like sales (Harbor, Midtown, Eastgate; Northside excluded as it opened 2025-07-01) fell about 19.7% under the accounting week convention (Sun-Sat, 2026-04-05→2026-06-27 vs 2025-04-06→2025-06-28) and about 20.0% under the operations week convention (Sat-Fri, 2026-04-04→2026-06-26 vs 2025-04-05→2025-06-27).\nNUMBERS: {\"accounting_2026_sales\": 81625.85, \"accounting_2025_sales\": 101597.06, \"accounting_pct_change\": -19.66, \"operations_2026_sales\": 81043.97, \"operations_2025_sales\": 101272.82, \"operations_pct_change\": -19.97, \"stores_included\": [\"location:S1\",\"location:S2\",\"location:S3\"], \"store_excluded_not_open_both_periods\": \"location:S4 (opened 2025-07-01)\"}\nEVIDENCE: metric:gross_sales v1, location:S1 assertions (id 1-2, valid_from 2025-01-01), location:S2 assertions (id 3-4, valid_from 2025-01-01), location:S3 assertions (id 5-6, valid_from 2025-01-01), location:S4 assertions (id 7-8, valid_from 2025-07-01), compute_metric calls filtered on order_line.rang_up_at for S1/S2/S3 over windows 2026-04-05..2026-06-28, 2025-04-06..2025-06-29, 2026-04-04..2026-06-27, 2025-04-05..2025-06-28\nACTIONS: none",
